{
  "name": "issue_1705_economizer_running_when_pause_turns_thermostat_off",
  "description": "Blower install: window cooling starts its blower during the open-window delay; when the pause then switches the thermostat from cool to Off, the blower keeps running",
  "source": "synthetic",
  "issue": 1705,
  "use_coordinator": true,
  "skip_startup_coalesce": true,
  "notes": [
    "Occupant: window cooling is running the blower while the thermostat is still in cool, and Climate Advisor's door/window pause then switches the thermostat from cool to Off. Before #1705 that pause asserted fan_mode auto (stopping window cooling's blower) and its real cool -> Off change cleared CA's blower flag, so the blower stopped and window cooling, still recorded in cool-down, never restarted it.",
    "Modelling: the coordinator's own 30-minute window-cooling check passes 'windows open' only once a window has passed its open-window delay, i.e. after the pause has landed, so in production this state arises when the pause is re-applied with window cooling already running (for example when the occupant's cool override during a pause ends). The scenario reaches it the short way: a direct economizer_check (the engine's public entry point) inside a 5-minute delay, with the pause landing at 19:55, before the coordinator's next check.",
    "Humidity is dry throughout (outdoor 70F at 49.1% = 50F dew point), so the #1691 humid-air guard never blocks the start.",
    "Three-exercise protocol (CLAUDE.md Sec 10): (a) effectiveness: this is the scenario that needs the economizer exemption in the #89 clear (the pause's cool -> Off is a real change to Off, so the off -> off check does not help) and the economizer guard on _set_hvac_mode('off')'s fan_mode auto assert; removing either one alone fails it (verified by mutation). (b) docs-production: docs/fan-lifecycle-spec.md 'Thermostat Off Clears CA's Blower Flag Only on a Real Change to Off (Issue #1705)' states both rules and production applies them. (c) occupant: if this regressed, a window opened while the AC is on would lose its free blower cooling as soon as the pause lands."
  ],
  "verdict": {
    "type": "positive",
    "summary": "Pause after window cooling started keeps the blower",
    "observed_behavior": "economizer cool-down, blower on",
    "expected_behavior": "economizer cool-down, blower on"
  },
